why A wand of your school for the 30s: frost, arcane or fire.

# Tabetha's wand chain, both factions: Journey to the Marsh (1947), Hidden
# Secrets (1949), Get the Scoop (1950), Rituals of Power (1951), Items of Power
# (1948) and Mage's Wand (1952).
# Levels 30-40: the Forever beta stops at 30 until launch on 4 November, so
# this guide is based on data, not play.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the chain,
# "Plucky" Johnson's spot, the Witherbark trolls and the Bolt Charged Bramble;
# Forever's Mage class quest list
# (data/local/quest-audit/, all six unchanged) and
# quest data (quests 1947 to 1952, checked
# 2026-10-14) for the givers and the reward choice (Icefury, Nether Force or
# Ragefire Wand); the quest texts for Tabetha's cottage and the Scarlet
# Monastery; codex/instances.json for the Scarlet Monastery Library entrance.
# The KB drops table: Witherbark Totem Stick 40% from every Witherbark troll
# (level 30-36), Jade 20% from the Torn Fin Coastrunners (level 29) south-west
# of Southshore. data/local/mechanics (quest-steps and quest-notes, checked
# 2026-10-20): the /beckon and the phrase, Plucky's 5 minute respawn, the
# Outer (not Inner) Binding circle and its three elementals, the bramble's
# 10 second wait and its loss on death, the book beside Compendium of the
# Fallen in the Library's last hallway, the level 38-41 elites on the east
# side of Tabetha's farm.
# Items of Power opens with Journey to the Marsh (quests.json pre 1947), so it
# is taken on the first visit to Tabetha and the Arathi part fits the trip
# east for the Scarlet Monastery. Mage's Wand needs both 1948 and 1951.
# Rituals of Power is dungeon work: the book lies in the Scarlet Monastery
# Library (a group of five, level 33-41).

step Journey to the Marsh (Stormwind)
  only Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Jennea Cannon at the top of the Wizard's Sanctum, Stormwind's Mage Quarter, sends you to Tabetha; Bink in Ironforge gives the same quest.
  level 30
  accept 1947 npc 5497                        -- Jennea Cannon

step Journey to the Marsh (Orgrimmar)
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Deino, one of Orgrimmar's mage trainers in Darkbriar Lodge, sends you to Tabetha; Anastasia Hartwell in the Undercity and Ursyn Ghull in Thunder Bluff give the same quest.
  level 30
  accept 1947 npc 5885                        -- Deino

step Tabetha
  zone Dustwallow Marsh
  tip Tabetha, a hermit, lives in a cottage deep in the marsh west of Theramore, just north of the Stonemaul Ruins. Level 38-41 elites roam the east side of her farm, and swimming in passes level 42 Muckshells: come in from the west along the road from the Barrens. Her cottage is no refuge: mobs follow you inside. Take both her quests.
  turnin 1947                                 -- Tabetha
  accept 1949
  accept 1948

step Magus Tirth
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip Magus Tirth spends his days at the race track in the Shimmering Flats, south-east Thousand Needles.
  turnin 1949                                 -- Magus Tirth
  accept 1950

step "Plucky" Johnson
  tip Tirth's apprentice is "Plucky" Johnson, a small grey chicken pecking around the foot of the race track's lookout tower; at night type /target plucky. Target him and type /beckon (not /chicken or /wave): he turns human for a moment. Talk to him and ask for the phrase. Do not attack him. If he is gone, he is back within 5 minutes.
  complete 1950 @79.6,75.6                    -- "Plucky" Johnson
  turnin 1950                                 -- Magus Tirth
  accept 1951

step Witherbark trolls and the Bolt Charged Bramble
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip The Witherbark trolls (level 30-36) hold the villages in south-eastern Arathi and south of Hammerfall; every kind of them drops a Witherbark Totem Stick about two times in five: you need ten. Then go to the Circle of Outer Binding (the outer one, not the Inner circle). Three elementals (level 33-39) stand around its middle stone: pull them one at a time and clear them first. Stand at the middle stone and use a totem stick; about ten seconds later the Bolt Charged Bramble forms on the stone: click it. If you die before you pick it up, the bramble and the sticks are lost and you need ten more.
  collect 7273 x10                            -- Witherbark Totem Stick
  use 7273 quest 1948.2 @52.04,50.74          -- at the middle stone of the Circle of Outer Binding
  collect 7272 quest 1948.2 @52.04,50.74      -- Bolt Charged Bramble

step Jade
  tip Tabetha also wants one Jade, a green gem. Miners sometimes find one in ore veins; the Auction House sells it; the Torn Fin Coastrunners on the coast south-west of Southshore drop one about every fifth kill. Do not sell it to a vendor by mistake.
  collect 1529 quest 1948.1                   -- Jade

step Rituals of Power
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Tirth sold the book to the Scarlet Crusade. The Scarlet Monastery stands in north-eastern Tirisfal Glades; take the Library wing with a group of five. The book is in the last long hallway, the one that ends in Arcanist Doan's round room: on the left-hand shelf as you face his room, next to the Compendium of the Fallen. Take the thick, highlighted blue book sticking out of the shelf; a magnifying-glass cursor means a book you can only read.
  collect 7274 quest 1951.1 @82.6,33.8        -- Rituals of Power: Scarlet Monastery Library

step Tabetha's ritual
  zone Dustwallow Marsh
  tip Back to Tabetha. With both quests handed in she starts the ritual: wait a few seconds, then talk to her again and pick your wand: Icefury (frost), Nether Force (arcane) or Ragefire (fire).
  turnin 1951                                 -- Tabetha
  turnin 1948
  accept 1952
  turnin 1952 choose 7514 11263 7513          -- Mage's Wand
